<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Pep lifts yr shr, div increased.</title>
<headline>Pep lifts yr shr, div increased.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>16 months to June 30 vs 12 months to February 28</p>
<p>		 (million Namibian dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)		28.0     vs    19.3</p>
<p>    Div (cts)	   7.5 making 11.0     vs    8.5</p>
<p>Net profit after tax</p>
<p>     and outside shareholders     9.1     vs    6.3</p>
<p>    Turnover			  132.2     vs    94.5</p>
<p>Div payable November 1</p>
<p>on register October 18</p>
<p>Full name: Pep Namibia Holdings</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said drought and higher interest rates hit profits but higher income from investments and less tax cushioned losses.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
